WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.169 --> 00:00:06.330
Hello and welcome to this video on the exercise setup.

2
00:00:06.330 --> 00:00:13.330
So in this video we're just going to go through and we're going to get ourselves ready so that we can do the exercise.

3
00:00:13.330 --> 00:00:17.969
So to start with I am going to fire up the Epic Launcher.

4
00:00:17.969 --> 00:00:21.969
And then I'm going to go over to the library tab here.

5
00:00:21.969 --> 00:00:29.920
And I'm going to hit launch on the engine version 5.32

6
00:00:29.920 --> 00:00:35.170
which is the latest as of the time of recording.

7
00:00:35.170 --> 00:00:38.299
You however can use any version you want to.

8
00:00:38.299 --> 00:00:40.299
I'm then going to wait for this to fire up.

9
00:00:40.299 --> 00:00:43.460
I'm then going to come under the games templates

10
00:00:43.460 --> 00:00:47.740
and I'm going to select the third person template.

11
00:00:47.740 --> 00:00:51.740
I'm selecting this because this will have a skeletal mesh

12
00:00:51.740 --> 00:00:54.740
and a whole load of animations that we can use.

13
00:00:54.740 --> 00:01:01.840
I'll just leave the project on blueprint

14
00:01:01.840 --> 00:01:05.450
and then place it somewhere and hit the create button.

15
00:01:05.450 --> 00:01:10.450
Once this has fired up you should see a project which looks a little bit like this.

16
00:01:10.450 --> 00:01:13.510
Now if I was to hit play

17
00:01:13.510 --> 00:01:18.459
you can see that we have Quinn here

18
00:01:18.459 --> 00:01:21.459
and she is already fully animated

19
00:01:21.459 --> 00:01:23.459
and can move around the level.

20
00:01:23.459 --> 00:01:30.370
I am going to want to disconnect that.

21
00:01:30.370 --> 00:01:35.200
So I'm going to come down into the content browser

22
00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:44.290
and I will dock the content browser in the layout.

23
00:01:44.290 --> 00:01:51.819
Now I'm going to go to the content directory within the project.

24
00:01:51.819 --> 00:01:53.819
Right hand click.

25
00:01:53.819 --> 00:01:56.819
And I'm going to create a new folder.

26
00:01:56.819 --> 00:02:06.939
And I'm going to call this my-animation-blueprints.

27
00:02:06.939 --> 00:02:15.500
I'm just going to use this directory so that I can just find all the files that I'm working.

28
00:02:15.500 --> 00:02:18.500
I will jump into the my-animation-blueprint directory.

29
00:02:18.500 --> 00:02:20.500
Right hand click.

30
00:02:20.500 --> 00:02:22.500
And under animation

31
00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:26.500
we have a selection for animation blueprint.

32
00:02:26.500 --> 00:02:28.729
When I select that

33
00:02:28.729 --> 00:02:31.729
it's not going to automatically create the blueprint.

34
00:02:31.729 --> 00:02:35.729
It's going to ask me to specify a skeleton.

35
00:02:35.729 --> 00:02:41.340
And in this case I'm going to use the SK underscore mannequin.

36
00:02:41.340 --> 00:02:44.139
And I'm going to push create.

37
00:02:44.139 --> 00:02:57.629
Now I will name this my-animation-BP.

38
00:02:57.629 --> 00:02:59.629
I've just prefixed it with my.

39
00:02:59.629 --> 00:03:03.659
And you'll see me do this a fair amount during the exercise.

40
00:03:03.659 --> 00:03:07.659
I'm just doing this because it helps me identify the files that I'm working with.

41
00:03:07.659 --> 00:03:11.460
I'm going to come back to the content directory.

42
00:03:11.460 --> 00:03:17.460
I'm going to go into the third person directory and into the blueprint directory.

43
00:03:17.460 --> 00:03:23.000
And here you will find the BP third person character.

44
00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:28.419
Now I am going to duplicate this third person character.

45
00:03:28.419 --> 00:03:34.710
And I'm going to put a my at the beginning here.

46
00:03:34.710 --> 00:03:40.710
And I'm going to move that blueprint into the my-animation-BP directory.

47
00:03:40.710 --> 00:03:48.389
This means that we have our own character pawn to work with.

48
00:03:48.389 --> 00:03:53.860
Now in the world settings

49
00:03:53.860 --> 00:03:55.860
I am going to come down to the game mode.

50
00:03:55.860 --> 00:03:57.860
Do the drop down.

51
00:03:57.860 --> 00:04:01.139
And with the default pawn class

52
00:04:01.139 --> 00:04:09.669
I'm going to change that to my third person character.

53
00:04:09.669 --> 00:04:15.740
So that means that we've now using the new blueprint as our pawn class.

54
00:04:15.740 --> 00:04:17.740
One last thing I want to do.

55
00:04:17.740 --> 00:04:21.740
And that is jump in and double click on the third person character.

56
00:04:21.740 --> 00:04:27.699
This will open up the blueprint for the third person character.

57
00:04:27.699 --> 00:04:29.699
I will dock it at the top here.

58
00:04:29.699 --> 00:04:33.730
And in the components I'm going to find the skeletal mesh.

59
00:04:33.730 --> 00:04:40.579
And you'll be able to see under animation

60
00:04:40.579 --> 00:04:45.019
we have the animation class APQuinn.

61
00:04:45.019 --> 00:04:48.949
Now if I search for my

62
00:04:48.949 --> 00:04:53.110
I'm going to swap that over to my-animation-BP class.

63
00:04:53.110 --> 00:04:58.129
I'm going to compile and save.

64
00:04:58.129 --> 00:05:02.290
Now we'll find that we can still move around the world.

65
00:05:02.290 --> 00:05:04.290
And we can still jump up and down.

66
00:05:04.290 --> 00:05:10.449
However, we just have Quinn here in the aid pose.

67
00:05:10.449 --> 00:05:13.449
So there is no animation going on at all at this point.

68
00:05:13.449 --> 00:05:15.250
But that's great.

69
00:05:15.250 --> 00:05:19.250
Because this is what we can then use to build it all back again from scratch

70
00:05:19.250 --> 00:05:21.250
throughout the rest of the exercise.

71
00:05:21.250 --> 00:05:26.819
And with that we have finished the setup for the exercise.

72
00:05:26.819 --> 00:05:29.819
In the next video we'll be able to jump in

73
00:05:29.819 --> 00:05:33.819
and start creating our own animation blueprint from scratch.
